# Content Style (CRITICAL)

All user-visible text must read like it was written by an expert human content writer, never like AI output.

## Banned characters in ALL content

Never use these in any user-visible string (messages/*.json, content/docs/**, JSON-LD descriptions, text served by routes like llms.txt/auth.md, or strings rendered from .tsx):

- Em-dash `—` (U+2014)
- En-dash `–` (U+2013)
- Arrow `→` (U+2192)
- Never substitute with `--` or a floating hyphen either

Hyphens inside compound words are fine: `end-of-day`, `low-stock`, `sign-up`.

## How to rewrite instead

Vary by context; never apply one strategy mechanically:

```text
BAD:  Free forever plan — no credit card needed
GOOD: Free forever plan, no credit card needed

BAD:  Six ready reports — overview, profit, customers
GOOD: Six ready reports: overview, profit, customers

BAD:  Track stock in real time — never oversell again
GOOD: Track stock in real time. Never oversell again.

BAD:  Pending → Approved
GOOD: Pending to Approved   (prose)  |  Settings > Branding   (navigation paths)
```

## Fixed conventions

- Receipt/ledger mono labels use a middle dot: `NO. 01 · WHAT YOU GET`
- Table "not included" marker is `[✗]`, never `[—]`
- Docs navigation paths use `>`: "Settings > Branding"
- Status flows in docs: "Pending, then Preparing, then Ready" or "moves through X, Y, and Z"

## Voice

- Punchy, confident, concrete. Short sentences over long ones.
- Arabic copy: Modern Standard Arabic with the file's existing light Egyptian flavor (شوف، اللي، مش). Match the register of surrounding strings; do not formalize casual copy or casualize formal copy.
- Keep SEO keywords intact when editing (free POS, free cashier, كاشير مجاني, متجر إلكتروني مجاني).
